module calculus.

use algebra.
use lists.

export differentiate, integrate, limit, series, converges, derive, antiderivative.

we define differentiate(expression) = kernelDifferentiate(expression).

we define differentiate(expression, variable) = kernelDifferentiate(expression, variable).

we define integrate(expression) = kernelIntegrate(expression).

we define integrate(expression, variable) = kernelIntegrate(expression, variable).

we define integrate(expression, lower, upper) = kernelIntegrate(expression, lower, upper).

we define integrate(expression, variable, lower, upper) = kernelIntegrate(expression, variable, lower, upper).

we define limit(expression, point) = kernelLimit(expression, point).

we define limit(expression, point, side) = kernelLimit(expression, point, side).

we define limit(expression, variable, point, side) = kernelLimit(expression, variable, point, side).

we define series(expression, point, order) = kernelSeries(expression, point, order).

we define series(expression, point, order, evaluate) = kernelSeries(expression, point, order, evaluate).

we define series(expression, variable, point, order) = kernelSeries(expression, variable, point, order).

we define series(expression, variable, point, order, evaluate) = kernelSeries(expression, variable, point, order, evaluate).

we define converges(expression, point) = kernelConverges(expression, point).

we define converges(expression, variable, point) = kernelConverges(expression, variable, point).

we define productOf(items) = fold(fn(acc, item) => acc * item, 1, items).

we define d(plus(a, rest...))/dx = d(a)/dx + fold(fn(acc, term) => acc + d(term)/dx, 0, list(rest)).

we define d(negate(u))/dx = -d(u)/dx.

we define d(times(a, rest...))/dx = let restProduct = productOf(list(rest)) in d(a)/dx * restProduct + a * d(restProduct)/dx.

we define d(power(u, n))/dx = n * power(u, n - 1) * d(u)/dx, where isNumber(n) && floor(n) == n.

we define d(sin(u))/dx = cos(u) * d(u)/dx.

we define d(cos(u))/dx = -sin(u) * d(u)/dx.

we define d(tan(u))/dx = d(u)/dx / power(cos(u), 2).

we define d(exp(u))/dx = exp(u) * d(u)/dx.

we define d(ln(u))/dx = d(u)/dx / u.

we define d(sqrt(u))/dx = d(u)/dx / (2 * sqrt(u)).

we define d(asin(u))/dx = d(u)/dx / sqrt(1 - power(u, 2)).

we define d(acos(u))/dx = -d(u)/dx / sqrt(1 - power(u, 2)).

we define d(atan(u))/dx = d(u)/dx / (1 + power(u, 2)).

we define d(sinh(u))/dx = cosh(u) * d(u)/dx.

we define d(cosh(u))/dx = sinh(u) * d(u)/dx.

we define d(tanh(u))/dx = d(u)/dx / power(cosh(u), 2).

we define d(asinh(u))/dx = d(u)/dx / sqrt(1 + power(u, 2)).

we define d(acosh(u))/dx = d(u)/dx / sqrt(power(u, 2) - 1).

we define d(atanh(u))/dx = d(u)/dx / (1 - power(u, 2)).

we define d(expression)/dx = differentiate(expression, x).

we define a(v, x) = power(v, 2) / 2, where same(v, x).

we define a(plus(first, rest...), x) = a(first, x) + fold(fn(acc, term) => acc + a(term, x), 0, list(rest)).

we define a(negate(u), x) = -a(u, x).

we define a(times(c, rest...), x) = c * a(productOf(list(rest)), x), where isNumber(c).

we define a(power(v, -1), v) = ln(v).

we define a(power(v, n), v) = power(v, n + 1) / (n + 1), where isNumber(n) && floor(n) == n.

we define a(exp(v), v) = exp(v).

we define a(sin(v), v) = -cos(v).

we define a(cos(v), v) = sin(v).

we define a(tan(v), v) = -ln(cos(v)).

we define a(ln(v), v) = v * ln(v) - v.

we define a(sqrt(v), v) = (2 / 3) * power(v, 3 / 2).

we define a(asin(v), v) = v * asin(v) + sqrt(1 - power(v, 2)).

we define a(acos(v), v) = v * acos(v) - sqrt(1 - power(v, 2)).

we define a(atan(v), v) = v * atan(v) - ln(1 + power(v, 2)) / 2.

we define a(expression, x) = integrate(expression, x).

we define derive(expression, variable) = derivative(expression, variable).

we define antiderivative(expression, variable) = a(expression, variable).

theorem derivative_of_sine.
for every expression u in x,
d(sin(u))/dx = cos(u) * d(u)/dx.
proof:
by the definition of d.
end proof.

end module.
